{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116024",
      "title": "Angular Has Multiple Injectors!",
      "lectureOrder": 182,
      "videoOrder": 174,
      "sourceHash": "42bba53975dd94fdd1cef5c162467b025a586f20e1079d5e158b85b0a9b2c5c8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.84,
          "end": 3.87,
          "en": "So now that we got a working service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.87,
          "end": 6.6,
          "en": "it's time to dive deeper into services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.6,
          "end": 10.02,
          "en": "and most importantly, dependency injection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.02,
          "end": 13.26,
          "en": "because services in the end are about creating such classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.26,
          "end": 17.1,
          "en": "which can have shared data or shared logic, or both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.1,
          "end": 18.36,
          "en": "That's basically it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.36,
          "end": 20.46,
          "en": "The interesting part then instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.46,
          "end": 23.4,
          "en": "is how you can make Angular aware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.4,
          "end": 26.25,
          "en": "of those injectable services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.25,
          "end": 29.04,
          "en": "And one way of making Angular aware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.04,
          "end": 31.29,
          "en": "and arguably the most important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.29,
          "end": 36,
          "en": "and common way is to use this @Injectable decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36,
          "end": 39.033,
          "en": "with providedIn set two root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.87,
          "end": 43.92,
          "en": "But as it turns out, that's not the only way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.92,
          "end": 46.59,
          "en": "of providing an injectable value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.59,
          "end": 49.53,
          "en": "and of making Angular aware of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.53,
          "end": 50.91,
          "en": "because you might recall",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.91,
          "end": 54.39,
          "en": "that I mentioned these different injectors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.39,
          "end": 56.64,
          "en": "which are managed by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.64,
          "end": 59.49,
          "en": "and I mentioned that I would come back to them later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.49,
          "end": 61.293,
          "en": "Well, now is later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.25,
          "end": 67.25,
          "en": "The idea behind these injectors is that Angular has them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.44,
          "end": 72.06,
          "en": "to register values that can be requested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.06,
          "end": 74.61,
          "en": "by components, directives or services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.61,
          "end": 76.56,
          "en": "So it's these injectors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.56,
          "end": 78.45,
          "en": "to which these components, directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.45,
          "end": 82.743,
          "en": "and services reach out in the end if they need a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.06,
          "end": 89.03999999999999,
          "en": "And these injectors are also set up as a hierarchy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.03999999999999,
          "end": 91.83,
          "en": "with the platform injector at the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.83,
          "end": 95.13,
          "en": "Technically, there is a NullInjector above that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.13,
          "end": 97.47,
          "en": "which always returns an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.47,
          "end": 99.93,
          "en": "if you request a value from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.93,
          "end": 102.96000000000001,
          "en": "So it exists basically as a fallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.96000000000001,
          "end": 106.14,
          "en": "to generate an error in case you're requesting a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.14,
          "end": 109.35,
          "en": "that's not provided by any injector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.35,
          "end": 111.84,
          "en": "but that's therefore not really an injector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.84,
          "end": 113.16,
          "en": "that provides a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.16,
          "end": 115.47,
          "en": "Instead, it will just generate errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.47,
          "end": 118.53,
          "en": "if you are not providing a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.53,
          "end": 122.49,
          "en": "So these are instead the important injectors here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.49,
          "end": 123.84,
          "en": "And the idea behind them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.84,
          "end": 127.98,
          "en": "is that the platform injector could provide values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.98,
          "end": 132.45,
          "en": "service instances, for example, for multiple applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.45,
          "end": 136.17000000000002,
          "en": "that are registered in one Angular project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.17000000000002,
          "end": 138.27,
          "en": "which is a more advanced use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.27,
          "end": 139.89,
          "en": "and which is not something we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.89,
          "end": 143.04,
          "en": "in our demo application here, but in main.ts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.04,
          "end": 145.95,
          "en": "you could bootstrap multiple applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.95,
          "end": 149.04,
          "en": "and it would then be the platform injector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.04,
          "end": 152.07,
          "en": "that could provide a single instance of a service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.07,
          "end": 156.12,
          "en": "for example, for multiple independent applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.12,
          "end": 159.87,
          "en": "But more relevant for most Angular applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.87,
          "end": 164.43,
          "en": "are the application root EnvironmentInjector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.43,
          "end": 166.8,
          "en": "potentially the ModuleInjector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.8,
          "end": 169.32,
          "en": "if you are working with ngModules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.32,
          "end": 171.93,
          "en": "which is something I'll get back to later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.93,
          "end": 173.433,
          "en": "and the ElementInjector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.96,
          "end": 177.93,
          "en": "and it's always the ElementInjector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.93,
          "end": 181.26,
          "en": "to which a component reaches out first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.26,
          "end": 185.43,
          "en": "for example, to request a dependency,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.43,
          "end": 187.413,
          "en": "a service instance, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.31,
          "end": 191.49,
          "en": "And if it doesn't get one from there, it moves up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.49,
          "end": 194.824,
          "en": "to the application root EnvironmentInjector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.824,
          "end": 196.89,
          "en": "or the ModuleInjector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.89,
          "end": 199.77,
          "en": "And if it doesn't get a service instance from there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.77,
          "end": 202.38,
          "en": "it moves up to the platform injector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.38,
          "end": 205.05,
          "en": "And if it doesn't get one from there, it moves up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.05,
          "end": 208.77,
          "en": "to that NullInjector and gets an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.77,
          "end": 212.22,
          "en": "And you can see that error in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.22,
          "end": 216.36,
          "en": "if you disable this Injectable decorator here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 216.36,
          "end": 219.003,
          "en": "on this TasksService class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.1,
          "end": 222.72,
          "en": "With that change made,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.72,
          "end": 226.17000000000002,
          "en": "and that's the only change I made here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.17000000000002,
          "end": 229.98,
          "en": "you will see that now the application seems to crash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.98,
          "end": 231.66,
          "en": "and if you open your developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.66,
          "end": 234.9,
          "en": "you'll see an error here from the NullInjector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 234.9,
          "end": 237.27,
          "en": "which I mentioned, which in the end tells us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 237.27,
          "end": 241.14,
          "en": "that we requested an instance of the TasksService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 241.14,
          "end": 243.333,
          "en": "but we got no provider for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 244.29,
          "end": 246.3,
          "en": "And that's the job of the NullInjector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 246.3,
          "end": 250.35,
          "en": "It generates those errors in case we're requesting something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 250.35,
          "end": 252.81,
          "en": "which we're not providing anywhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 252.81,
          "end": 255.3,
          "en": "and we aren't providing this service anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 255.3,
          "end": 258.24,
          "en": "because I removed this annotation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 258.24,
          "end": 261.963,
          "en": "So how else could we provide it?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
